  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4c5a24e4-2130-4cb9-a292-f9af235512dd" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(c=\frac t{48}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(c = 48t\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c=\\frac t{48}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c = t-48\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c=\\frac t3\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>5. Choose the equation that represents the number of teaspoons, <emphasis>t</emphasis>, contained in a cup, <emphasis>C</emphasis>.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5cc7c5b1-deb6-422d-998d-0274bdde0e79" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(b=\frac q{32}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(b=\\frac q{32}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b=\\frac q{12}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b=\\frac q{64}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b=32q\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>6. The volume of dry goods, like apples or peaches, can be measured using bushels, pecks, and quarts. A bushel contains 4 pecks, and a peck contains 8 quarts.<emphasis>b</emphasis>, and the number of quarts, <emphasis>q</emphasis>? </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
